  "issue": {
    "body": "Suppose I have my application reverse proxied, such that http://my.domain/foo (e.g. Traefik or Nginx) has the upstream http://localhost:8000 (the Starlette app). `url_for` will generate urls relative to the upstream url. How do I make it produce urls relative to the external url (with prefix /foo)?\r\n\r\nFor other projects, e.g. Flask/Werkzeug, this can be handled by setting `SCRIPT_NAME` in the request environment (scope) if the 'X-Forwarded-Prefix' header is set. It does not look like there is an equivalent option in Starlette.\r\n\r\nAm I missing something? Otherwise, consider this a feature request.",
    "closed_at": "2019-11-01T14:11:01Z",
    "created_at": "2019-08-18T06:44:20Z",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/604",
    "number": 604,
    "state": "closed",
    "title": "Starlette behind reverse proxy, url_for does not return externally valid urls",
    "user": "narzeja"
  },
  "repository": "Kludex/starlette",
